  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (config_045) is the clear best at 0.725 accuracy, and all other variables (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion) are well-characterized. The remaining uncertainty is whether the image encoder choice (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) contributes meaningfully when paired with the strong scvi_n200 RNA encoder. config_035 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) isolates the image encoder variable while holding all other settings at their best-known values. This is the best use of experiment 8 because: (1) it directly tests whether the ~2-3% gap seen between imagenet_vit_l and resnet50 in the scgpt setting persists with scvi_n200, (2) if it performs close to config_045, it broadens the set of viable configurations for the final experiment, and (3) if it performs significantly worse, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is critical and the last experiment should focus on confirming config_045 or a minor perturbation. With only 2 experiments remaining, reducing uncertainty about the image encoder's marginal contribution is the highest-value information gain."
}

